// Copy this file to Secrets.xcconfig for local builds (the copy is git-ignored).
// Put YOUR Apple team and unique identifiers here. There is no API key in this
// file on purpose: the DashScope key is entered in the app's Settings screen.
//
// The keyboards share data with the app through the App Group, and the app's
// Keychain item is tied to its bundle identifier: keep these stable once you
// have installed a build, or the keyboards lose their settings and the app its key.
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOUR_TEAM_ID
VELIKIY_MOGUCHIY_APP_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = com.example.velikiy-moguchiy
VELIKIY_MOGUCHIY_KEYBOARD_RU_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = com.example.velikiy-moguchiy.keyboard.ru
VELIKIY_MOGUCHIY_KEYBOARD_EN_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = com.example.velikiy-moguchiy.keyboard.en
VELIKIY_MOGUCHIY_KEYBOARD_KK_RU_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = com.example.velikiy-moguchiy.keyboard.kk.ru
VELIKIY_MOGUCHIY_KEYBOARD_KK_EN_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = com.example.velikiy-moguchiy.keyboard.kk.en
VELIKIY_MOGUCHIY_WIDGET_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = com.example.velikiy-moguchiy.widgets
VELIKIY_MOGUCHIY_APP_GROUP_IDENTIFIER = group.com.example.velikiy-moguchiy

// Different values for Debug and Release are possible with a condition, e.g.:
// VELIKIY_MOGUCHIY_APP_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER[config=Release] = com.example.velikiy-moguchiy.sideload
//
// Scripts/build-ipa.sh fills $(AppIdentifierPrefix) of the ad-hoc IPA with
// TEAM_PREFIX from the environment, or with DEVELOPMENT_TEAM from this file.
//
// Upgrading from the working name: these settings were called GOVORUN_*.
// Rename them once, keeping your values:
//   sed -i '' 's/^GOVORUN_/VELIKIY_MOGUCHIY_/' Config/Secrets.xcconfig
// Identifiers that used to be written in Config/Debug.xcconfig and Release.xcconfig
// themselves now belong here, as [config=Debug] / [config=Release] lines, so that an
// installed build keeps its Keychain item, App Group data and keyboards.
// The Scripts/ tools stop with a message while GOVORUN_* lines are left.
